    11	5. **H1’s proposed shortcut is broader than its cited rule.** [Plan line 90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:90) leans toward merging because the same annual-report note checks both amounts. A single document can report two independently moving amounts. The standard requires the *same result* to settle both and also requires scope to distinguish financing from guarantees ([standard, lines 293–294 and 316–319](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:293)). D210’s one-deal-or-programme wording does not establish that sharing a note makes two questions identical ([D210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2670)).
    12	
    13	6. **H2 describes a later question without yet showing how it survives until then.** [Plan lines 91 and 171](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:91) merge a later deadline into an earlier question, then propose opening a successor after expiry. The earlier question keeps its fixed deadline and outcomes ([PRD 06, lines 74–75](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/06-views.md:74)); the present succession path acts when matching a candidate ([code](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:284)). The plan leaves the later deadline’s preservation and the event that creates the successor to a future table. Without those, Kyber’s 2028 question can be lost if no new article arrives after 2027.
    14	
    15	7. **The holdout repair is incomplete.** [Plan lines 111–113](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:111) give the holdout only one blind labeller, so there is no second independent label with which to identify the “disagreements” it says Alex will decide. The working rule requires a blind second reader and recorded resolution ([AGENTS, lines 246–251](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/AGENTS.md:246)). Also, the plan does not say how holdout results stay out of subsequent tuning when each arm is measured. The separation of the author from the labels is an improvement, but it does not yet establish that control.
    16	
    17	8. **The first-50 summary repeats a source’s arithmetic error.** [Plan lines 8–9 and 80](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:8) report four borderline questions. Counting the actual rows in [the earlier gold](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-admission-v12-2026-10-26/docs/research/2026-10-28-quality-review/gold-admission.md:15) gives **23 keep, 12 duplicate, 10 do not open, and 5 borderline**; its summary line says 24 and 4. The 22 duplicate-or-do-not-open labels are correct as that reader’s judgments, but they remain unapproved judgments rather than established defects.
    18	
    19	I re-ran the corrected census read-only: **122 candidates, 39 merges and 2 successions** for the sealed ledger, and **32 candidates, 12 merges and 1 succession** for v38. The reported evidence counts match the census outputs, subject to the plan’s correct qualification that “same claim” labels are estimates. H3 now names the conflicting milestone rule; H4 is presented as a choice; and H7’s lean preserves D204. I did not independently verify every cost estimate, every archived verdict classification, or every factual claim in the plan.
    20	
    21	**Serious findings remain**, chiefly the gold’s coverage and the acceptance checks’ ability to pass a wrong destination. No files were edited.
