     1	"""The matching step answered by Jev instead of a generative call (log row 34). For each candidate: its relation to every
     2	thesis on its list (one `choice` per thesis) and its membership of every visible research group (one `noul` per group);
     3	for each incoming piece of evidence: its relation to every stored piece on its list under each linked thesis (one
     4	`choice` per stored piece). Code turns the probabilities into an answer in the matching schema, so `matching.check` and
     5	`writing.write` run unchanged: `merge` when a listed open thesis is the same quantity or event, `succession` when a
     6	listed thesis carries the same key for an earlier period and has no successor, else `new`; `repeat` when a stored
     7	piece is the same statement, `replace` when the incoming piece supersedes it, else `new`. Dependencies are not asked.
     8	Thresholds are pre-set (0.5); a membership above the threshold is added to the candidate's group references."""
